ts_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-uspenskiy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-uspenskiy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":9,"created_at":"2020-02-07T06:08:57Z","updated_at":"2020-03-09T19:18:28Z","closed_at":"2020-03-09T19:18:28Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"This is an error seen on debug build only.\r\n\r\nTo reproduce:\r\n```\r\nyugabyte=# create table pk(b int, a int, y int, x int, primary key(a, b));\r\nCREATE TABLE\r\nyugabyte=# create unique index on pk(x, y);\r\nCREATE INDEX\r\nyugabyte=# insert into pk(a,b,x,y) values(1,10,100,1000);\r\nyugabyte=# create table fk_primary(id int primary key, b int, a int, foreign key(a, b) references pk(a, b));\r\nCREATE TABLE\r\nyugabyte=# create table fk_unique(id int primary key, y int, x int, foreign key(x, y) references pk(x, y));\r\nCREATE TABLE\r\nyugabyte=# insert into pk(a,b,x,y) values(2,20,200,2000);\r\nINSERT 0 1\r\nyugabyte=# begin;\r\nBEGIN\r\nyugabyte=# INSERT INTO fk_unique(id, y, x) VALUES(2000, 2000, 200);\r\nINSERT 0 1\r\nyugabyte=# UPDATE pk SET x=201, y=2001 WHERE x=200 AND y=2000;\r\nserver closed the connection unexpectedly\r\n\tThis probably means the server terminated abnormally\r\n\tbefore or while processing the request.\r\nThe connection to the server was lost. Attempting reset: Failed.\r\n!> exit\r\n\r\n```\r\nNote that the error only happens if both tables have FK references. Changing the above to use just 1 FK reference (by removing fk_primary table) won't cause the error.","closed_by":{"login":"d-uspenskiy","id":47734295,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzM0Mjk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47734295?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.c